# Sakhi Clinic — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and fill in real values before
# building/deploying. Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to client
# code (see https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode.html) -- a variable with
# that prefix ends up inlined in the built JS bundle, so a real secret must
# NEVER be given a VITE_ name. See the "Server-only" section below for the
# one variable in this project that this actually applies to.
#
# Nothing in this file is required for the app to run. Every feature here
# degrades honestly when unset: Google Drive backup stays hidden behind a
# "not configured" state and local (on-device) backups are unaffected.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Drive backup (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OAuth 2.0 Client ID from Google Cloud Console (APIs & Services >
# Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID > Application type:
# Web application). Add this app's real origin(s) as an authorized
# JavaScript origin AND "<origin>/oauth/google/callback" as an authorized
# redirect URI. Full walkthrough: docs/GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md
#
# Leaving this unset is a fully supported configuration: the app runs
# normally with local-only backups and the Settings page shows Google
# Drive as "Not configured" rather than a broken "Connect" button.
VITE_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Drive backup -- server-only (required once VITE_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID above is set)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google's "Web application" OAuth client type requires client_secret on
# every token exchange, even with PKCE (see docs/GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md for
# why). This value is read ONLY by the two serverless functions
# api/oauth/google/exchange.ts and api/oauth/google/refresh.ts -- it is
# never bundled into client-side JS, never sent to the browser, and never
# logged. That is also exactly why this variable does NOT start with
# VITE_: a VITE_ prefix would defeat the point entirely by inlining it into
# the public build. One shared name covers both endpoints (and any future
# Google integration reusing the same OAuth client) rather than a
# Drive-specific name -- see docs/GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md's "Why one shared
# env var" section.
#
# In local dev, `vercel dev` reads this from .env/.env.local like any other
# process.env variable. In production/preview, set it directly in the
# Vercel project's Environment Variables settings -- do not put a real
# value in any committed file.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Not required. The app only ever calls Drive API v3 with the doctor's own
# OAuth access token (Authorization: Bearer <token>), which is how Google
# expects a user-scoped drive.file request to be authenticated. A separate
# API key is Google's mechanism for unauthenticated/public requests, which
# this app never makes -- it is deliberately not read anywhere in the
# codebase. Listed here only so anyone following older Google API examples
# doesn't wonder why it's missing.
# VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Not required. No code path in this app reads an app-name env var --
# "Sakhi Clinic" is set directly as the OAuth consent screen's app name in
# Google Cloud Console during setup (docs/GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md), and as
# the PWA manifest name in vite.config.ts. Listed here for parity with
# common Google API quick-start templates.
# VITE_GOOGLE_APP_NAME=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build metadata (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides the version string shown in Settings > Application if you need
# it to differ from package.json's "version" field at build time.
# VITE_APP_VERSION=
